=== 15:40 PRE-REGISTRATION (C4) -- is a SEED on the per-workspace key a reproducible re-roll?
Change under test: settings.prompt_cache_seed (ZAKCODE_PROMPT_CACHE_SEED) folded into the ws-hash when non-empty; empty keeps the
seedless key (worktree /opt/zak-code-seed, PR to follow). Cell: C4 = C1 exactly (07-ttl-cache, 27B, flag ON, PIN_MODE=workspace,
temp 0, N=3, dumps on) plus ZAKCODE_PROMPT_CACHE_SEED=reroll-1; src rsynced to zc-01 only AFTER C3 completes (never mid-chain).
Predictions: P4 byte-identical 3/3 (the seed only changes the key VALUE; the mechanism is C1s). P5, moderate confidence: the C4
trajectory differs from C1s (different first response or different program) -- D1 saw 2 basins in 3 fresh keys, and a slot collision
is possible. Pass/fail of the C4 basin is NOT predicted: a re-roll is a re-roll.
Decision rules: R5 P4 holds -> the seed is a reproducible re-roll; ship it behind the flag (already implemented; the PR lands
regardless of P5, since same-seed reproducibility is the property being sold). R6 P4 fails -> the seed introduced variation the
hash cannot have; instrument or code defect; do not ship until found. R7 P5 fails (C4 program == C1 program) -> run one more cell
with seed reroll-2 (C4b) and report the collision rate honestly; R5 still decides shipping. R8 instrument refusals are not results.
